From da5b91f9e67d37609dc5e04563f91136688de2ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiushengming <qiushengming1@huawei.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 20:53:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 960/960] downstream: iommu/ummu: Add UB UMMU framework
 extensions

commit 0cef6d6794c38701cd14158b48ebe3ab31da6a26 openEuler.

Extend the downstream IOMMU and UMMU interfaces required by the
HiSilicon UB UMMU driver.

Add UMMU core interfaces for SVA operation, TID-based domain lookup,
shared TID allocation, device configuration, TLB walk invalidation and
SVA-separated page-table management. Add IOVA fill and drain helpers,
including support for caller-provided GFP flags.

Introduce the HiSilicon UMMU extension module to handle bypass-device
selection and permission-table block configuration from the kernel
command line. Enable KSVA by default and extend the generic IOMMU
interfaces with KSVA capability reporting, PLBI gathering and DMA
strict-mode querying.

Extend the IOMMUFD UAPI with UMMU nested translation and hardware
information formats, and advertise the IOPF, free-bit and PPLBI
capabilities. Export the additional MM and page-pool facilities needed
by the UMMU implementation.

Also add KABI reserve fields to the public UMMU structures, provide
stubs for disabled configurations, mark superseded UMMU SVA interfaces
as deprecated and improve the related kernel-doc documentation.

Signed-off-by: qiushengming <qiushengming1@huawei.com>
